<!DOCTYPE html><html><head><meta charset="UTF-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Career guidance | CareerLaunch</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="<%=request.getContextPath()%>/assets/style.css"></head><body><%@ include file="includes/header.jspf" %>
<main class="container page-space"><p class="eyebrow">PLAN YOUR NEXT STEP</p><h1>Career guidance</h1><p class="lead">Choose a path, build practical skills, and show what you can do with projects.</p><div class="roadmap-grid">
<article class="roadmap-card"><span class="roadmap-number">01</span><h2>Java Full Stack Developer</h2><p>Build complete web applications from database to interface.</p><h3>Learning roadmap</h3><ul><li>Core Java, OOP, collections and exceptions</li><li>SQL, MySQL and JDBC</li><li>Servlets, JSP and MVC architecture</li><li>HTML, CSS, JavaScript and Bootstrap</li><li>Git, testing and deployment</li></ul><p class="skills">Portfolio project: Job Portal</p></article>
<article class="roadmap-card"><span class="roadmap-number">02</span><h2>Backend Java Developer</h2><p>Focus on APIs, business logic, databases and secure services.</p><h3>Learning roadmap</h3><ul><li>Java fundamentals and data structures</li><li>JDBC, SQL joins and transactions</li><li>Servlets and HTTP</li><li>REST API concepts and JSON</li><li>Spring Boot as a next step</li></ul><p class="skills">Portfolio project: Inventory REST service</p></article>
<article class="roadmap-card"><span class="roadmap-number">03</span><h2>QA Automation Engineer</h2><p>Use programming to test software consistently and efficiently.</p><h3>Learning roadmap</h3><ul><li>Java fundamentals</li><li>Testing basics and test cases</li><li>Selenium WebDriver</li><li>JUnit or TestNG</li><li>Git and CI basics</li></ul><p class="skills">Portfolio project: Automated job search tests</p></article>
</div><section class="tip-box"><h2>Fresher interview checklist</h2><p>Prepare a 60-second project explanation, database schema, one challenging bug you solved, Java OOP concepts, SQL joins, and how your servlet communicates with the database.</p></section></main></body></html>